From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Netmojo Systems <56850867+netmojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] wifi: brcmfmac: report port authorization only after
 the connect result

asahi-7.2.12-2 reports port authorization for SAE and PSK twice when a
connection completes: once before cfg80211_connect_done(), and again after
it. cfg80211 expects association or roam to be reported first. On a first
connect, it drops the early event because the interface is not yet
connected. On a reassociation to a different BSSID, it checks the event
against the old BSSID and can reach a WARN_ON in sme.c.

Drop the early report. The one after cfg80211_connect_done() is unchanged.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index f9b390f..197d31f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -6723,12 +6723,6 @@ brcmf_bss_connect_done(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 		if (completed) {
 			brcmf_get_assoc_ies(cfg, ifp);
 			brcmf_update_bss_info(cfg, ifp);
-			if ((profile->use_fwsup == BRCMF_PROFILE_FWSUP_SAE) ||
-			    (profile->use_fwsup == BRCMF_PROFILE_FWSUP_PSK)) {
-				cfg80211_port_authorized(ndev, profile->bssid,
-							 NULL, 0, GFP_KERNEL);
-				brcmf_dbg(CONN, "Report port authorized\n");
-			}
 			set_bit(BRCMF_VIF_STATUS_CONNECTED,
 				&ifp->vif->sme_state);
 			conn_params.status = WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS;
-- 
2.0

